course: dictionary
lesson: 8130
title: Words that repeat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Repetitive means doing or saying the same thing again and again. Look at «Robots take over repetitive tasks, but people still design, build, fix and run them.» The clue is the word tasks: a task that is the same every time is repetitive.
explain: A repetitive job can be boring, because it never changes. In writing, repetitive means using the same words or sentence starts too many times, like «then … then … then». Your teacher wants you to vary your openers so your writing stays interesting.
explain: Repetition is not always bad. Poems and songs repeat lines on purpose, because the repeats make them catchy. So ask yourself: is the repeating helping the reader, or just getting boring?
fact: Repetitive means doing or saying the same thing again and again.
fact: A repetitive task is boring because it is the same every time.
fact: In writing, repetitive means using the same words or sentence starts too many times.
fact: «Machines take over repetitive tasks, while people design, build, fix and run them, and new jobs appear as old ones change.» Here repetitive tasks are the jobs machines can do over and over.
fact: Poems and songs sometimes repeat words on purpose, to make them memorable.
exercise: «Robots take over repetitive tasks, but people still design, build, fix and run them.» What does repetitive mean in this sentence? | Very difficult to understand | Hidden away and rarely seen | *Done again and again, the same every time | Done quickly and with great care
exercise: Your teacher writes «Then … then … then» in the margin of your story. Why? | You forgot to write the ending | Your story is too short | Your story is very exciting | *You have repeated the same sentence start too many times
exercise: Copy the word from «Machines take over repetitive tasks, while people design, build, fix and run them.» that tells you the tasks are the same over and over. | machines | *repetitive | people | design
test: Ella says a song with the same chorus three times is repetitive, so it must be bad. Is she right? | Yes, all repeating is bad | Yes, because songs should never have a chorus | No, because repetitive means very fast | *Not always, because songs repeat on purpose to make them catchy
test: «A repetitive pattern» means what? | A pattern that is never seen | *A pattern that keeps repeating the same way | A pattern made of big pictures | A pattern that changes every second
exam: Which sentence is repetitive? | The dog barked at the postman, who ran away. | Rain fell all afternoon, and the grass turned green. | *I went out. I went out. I went out. | I went to the park and then I played football.
